  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Prior approval for the change of use of the existing building from Class E (commercial) to Class C3 (dwellinghouses) to provide four self-contained residential units, together with associated internal alterations.&nbsp;",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;In the absence of a suitable undertaking to secure that the occupiers of the new residential units would not be able to apply for on street parking permits, the proposals would have an adverse impact on street parking conditions, highway safety,&amp;nbsp; sustainable modes of transport and would contribute to congestion in the surrounding area contrary to Policies T1 and T4 of the London Plan (2021) and Hackney Local Plan Policies LP43 and LP45. Having regard to The Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015, Part MA.2(2)(a), the change of use is not supported on the basis of adverse impact on on-street parking conditions and highway safety.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;﻿&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;﻿&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-1e49ace7-7fff-690c-f986-5154687b3098&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;The proposal would not satisfy the requirements of paragraph MA.2.(2)(f) of Class MA, Part 3 of Schedule 2 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended). The proposed development, by reason of poor levels of daylight, would provide a sub-standard form of accommodation to the detriment of future occupiers, contrary to policy D6 (Housing quality and standards) of the London Plan (2021), policies LP17 (Housing Design) of the Hackney Local Plan LP33 (2020).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
